;; wal-ingest.aura — ingestion API for fresh WAL segments
;;
;; Ingestion is the entry point for new segments into the pipeline. A caller
;; supplies a target tier (usually 'hot), the segment size in bytes, and the
;; current virtual clock; we mint a fresh segment record via (make-segment …)
;; from wal-types.aura, stamp it with the present (current-ms) timestamp,
;; and append it to the tier's segment store via (store-add! …) from
;; wal-store.aura. Each ingest is also recorded in the event log via
;; (log-event! 'ingest) from wal-log.aura so the stdout contract can show
;; the audit trail.
;;
;; Design notes:
;;   - ingest-segment! mutates the store in place (via store-add!) and returns
;;     the newly created segment so callers can chain further operations.
;;   - The segment id is derived from a small monotonic counter *ingest-id*.
;;     We don't expose a setter; ids are an implementation detail of ingestion.
;;   - We deliberately do NOT call (advance-ms!) here. Time advancement is the
;;     caller's responsibility — this keeps ingestion orthogonal to the clock.

;; Internal monotonic id counter. Stored as a one-element list so we can
;; use set! on its car, matching the pattern in wal-clock.aura / wal-log.aura.
(define *ingest-id* (list 0))

;; ingest-segment! : store bytes -> segment
;;
;; Mint a new segment of `bytes` size, stamp it at (current-ms), push it into
;; `store`, log the event, and return the new segment record.
;;
;; The id is assigned from the internal counter (1, 2, 3, ...). Tier is taken
;; from the store itself via (store-tier store) so we can never accidentally
;; ingest into the wrong tier symbol.
(define (ingest-segment! store bytes)
  (set! (car *ingest-id*) (+ (car *ingest-id*) 1))
  (let ((seg (make-segment (car *ingest-id*) bytes (current-ms) (store-tier store))))
    (store-add! store seg)
    (log-event! 'ingest)
    seg))
